; DLL search-order hardening (2026-09-24): crypt32.dll is not a KnownDLL, so
; it must not be a static import (see Makefile's DELAY_LIBS comment and
; src/main.c's SetDefaultDllDirectories/SetDllDirectoryW call). This lists
; only the symbols nutshell.exe actually calls -- statically-linked
; OpenSSL's Windows certificate-store loader (libcrypto.a's
; libdefault-lib-winstore_store.obj, pulled in by the default provider's
; store-loader table even though the app never asks for the "winstore:"
; scheme) -- so `dlltool --output-delaylib` can build a delay-import
; library for exactly what's used, no more. Hand-written, not gendef'd:
; gendef needs the real DLL and reads its whole export table, which is far
; more than this build calls.
;
; The last four are referenced only by OpenSSL's CAPI engine
; (libcrypto.a's libcrypto-lib-e_capi.obj), which the vcpkg build of
; OpenSSL used by the Linux cross-compile links in and the MSYS2 build on
; the Windows host does not. They are still delay-imported, never static;
; they resolve only if the engine is ever activated, which nutshell.exe
; never does.
LIBRARY crypt32.dll
EXPORTS
CertCloseStore
CertFindCertificateInStore
CertFreeCertificateContext
CertOpenSystemStoreW
CertDuplicateCertificateContext
CertEnumCertificatesInStore
CertGetCertificateContextProperty
CertOpenStore
